IMPORT prelude

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- employee share schemes taxed upfront (ss 83A-20, 83A-25,
-- 83A-30, 83A-33, 83A-35, 83A-45), the R&D tax offset of a small company (s 355-100) and the early stage investor tax offset
-- (ss 360-20, 360-25).
--
-- SEAT: the taxpayer -- an individual Australian resident: the employee who receives start-up ESS interests ("How is my
-- discount taxed?"), and the investor who buys shares in an early stage company ("What offset do I get?"). The R&D offset
-- belongs to the company; the founder asks it ("What R&D offset does my company get?"), a departure recorded in NOTES.md.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 267, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 79, 2026; register id
-- C2026C00400, 12 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.txt. The corporate tax rate the R&D offset
-- builds on comes from the Income Tax Rates Act 1986 s 23(2) (see itaa-income.l4) and is passed in.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The deferred-taxing route (Subdiv 83A-C) and the CGT treatment of ESS interests beyond their acquisition cost
-- (Subdiv 130-D); the broad-availability condition (s 83A-105(2)) and the share-trading integrity rule (s 83A-45(3)) as
-- anything but facts; foreign-source apportionment (s 83A-25(2)); the regulations under s 83A-315 that may substitute market
-- values. What an R&D entity, R&D activity or notional deduction is; the $150 million ceiling; the premium for larger entities
-- (s 355-100(1A)). The early stage innovation company test (s 360-40, the 100-point test in s 360-45) is one fact; the
-- modified CGT treatment of ESIC shares (Subdiv 360-B); carry-forward of the offset beyond the amount already counted.
-- Aggregated turnover (s 328-115) is a fact throughout.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 -- business and investment`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `83A-25, 83A-33, 83A-35, 83A-45 -- employee share schemes`

-- s 83A-25(1): "Your assessable income for the income year in which you acquire the *ESS interest includes the discount given in
-- relation to the interest."
-- s 83A-33 (start ups): reduce that amount for ESS interests to which (2)-(6), s 83A-45 and, for shares, s 83A-105(2) all apply:
--   (2) no equity interests in the company or its group "listed for quotation in the official list of any *approved stock
--       exchange";
--   (3) each company "incorporated ... less than 10 years before the end of the first company's most recent income year before
--       you acquired the interest";
--   (4) "an *aggregated turnover not exceeding $50 million for the company's most recent income year";
--   (5) for a share, "the discount on the ESS interest is no more than 15% of its *market value when you acquire it"; for a
--       right, "the amount that must be paid to exercise the right is greater than or equal to the market value of an ordinary
--       share";
--   (6) "your employer is an Australian resident".
-- s 83A-45: (1) employed by the company or a subsidiary; (2) the scheme relates only to ordinary shares; (3) not a share-trading
-- or investment company; (4)-(5) a minimum holding period during which disposal is not permitted; (6) no more than 10% of the
-- shares or votes.
-- s 83A-35 (other cases): (6) the scheme is "operated on a non-discriminatory basis in relation to at least 75% of the permanent
-- employees" with 3 years' service; (7) "no real risk" of forfeiture; (2)(a) "do not reduce the total amount by more than
-- $1,000"; (b) only if taxable income and the add-backs do "not exceed $180,000"; (c) not if s 83A-33 reduces the amount.
DECLARE EssInterest HAS
    `is a right rather than a share` IS A BOOLEAN
    `discount` IS A NUMBER
    `market value` IS A NUMBER
    `exercise price` IS A NUMBER
    `group has listed equity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years incorporated before the last income year end` IS A NUMBER
    `aggregated turnover last year` IS A NUMBER
    `employer is an Australian resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by the company or a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `scheme relates only to ordinary shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `share trading or investment company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `minimum holding period applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds more than 10 percent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `scheme broadly available` IS A BOOLEAN
    `scheme non-discriminatory for 75 percent of long-serving employees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no real risk of forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN
    `income for the 180000 test` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the interest` IS AN EssInterest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the market value condition is met` IF
    IF `the interest`'s `is a right rather than a share`
    THEN `the interest`'s `exercise price` AT LEAST `the interest`'s `market value`
    ELSE `the interest`'s `discount` TIMES 100 AT MOST `the interest`'s `market value` TIMES 15

GIVEN `the interest` IS AN EssInterest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the further conditions in 83A-45 are met` IF
        `the interest`'s `employed by the company or a subsidiary`
    AND `the interest`'s `scheme relates only to ordinary shares`
    AND (NOT `the interest`'s `share trading or investment company`)
    AND `the interest`'s `minimum holding period applies`
    AND (NOT `the interest`'s `holds more than 10 percent`)

@export Do my ESS interests get the start-up concession (s 83A-33)?
GIVEN `the interest` IS AN EssInterest @desc The shares or rights you acquired under the employee share scheme
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my ESS interests get the start-up concession` IF
        (NOT `the interest`'s `group has listed equity`)
    AND `the interest`'s `years incorporated before the last income year end` LESS THAN 10
    AND `the interest`'s `aggregated turnover last year` AT MOST 50000000
    AND `the market value condition is met` `the interest`
    AND `the interest`'s `employer is an Australian resident`
    AND `the further conditions in 83A-45 are met` `the interest`
    AND (`the interest`'s `is a right rather than a share` OR `the interest`'s `scheme broadly available`)

GIVEN `the interest` IS AN EssInterest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the other-cases reduction is available` IF
        `the interest`'s `scheme non-discriminatory for 75 percent of long-serving employees`
    AND `the interest`'s `no real risk of forfeiture`
    AND `the further conditions in 83A-45 are met` `the interest`
    AND `the interest`'s `income for the 180000 test` AT MOST 180000

@export How much of my ESS discount is in my assessable income this year (ss 83A-25, 83A-33, 83A-35)?
GIVEN `the interest` IS AN EssInterest @desc The shares or rights you acquired under the employee share scheme
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my ESS discount is assessable` MEANS
    IF `Do my ESS interests get the start-up concession` `the interest` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the other-cases reduction is available` `the interest`
         THEN `the interest`'s `discount` MINUS `the lesser of` 1000 (`the interest`'s `discount`)
         ELSE `the interest`'s `discount`

-- s 83A-30(1): "For the purposes of this Act (other than this Division), the *ESS interest ... is taken to have been acquired for
-- its *market value (rather than for its discounted value)." (2): not for a right whose discount the start-up concession reduced.
-- So for start-up shares the later capital gain is measured from market value at acquisition; for start-up rights, from what
-- was paid (the exercise price is a separate cost, not encoded).
@export For capital gains, what am I taken to have paid for my ESS interest (s 83A-30)?
GIVEN `the interest` IS AN EssInterest @desc The shares or rights you acquired under the employee share scheme
      `amount actually paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What you actually paid for the interest, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What am I taken to have paid for my ESS interest` MEANS
    IF `the interest`'s `is a right rather than a share` AND `Do my ESS interests get the start-up concession` `the interest`
    THEN `amount actually paid`
    ELSE `the interest`'s `market value`

§§ `355-100 -- R&D tax offset`

-- s 355-100(1), table item 1: "the *R&D entity's *aggregated turnover for the income year is less than $20 million (and item 2
-- of this table does not apply)" -- "the R&D entity's *corporate tax rate for the income year, plus 18.5 percentage points".
-- Item 2 (controlled by exempt entities) and item 3 ("any other case") -- "the R&D entity's *corporate tax rate", increased by the
-- premium in (1A) (not encoded). Note 1: "The tax offset will be a refundable tax offset if item 1 of the table applies".
-- s 355-100(2): if the total is less than $20,000, only the listed expenditure (research service providers, CRC contributions)
-- counts -- one fact here.
@export What is my company's R&D tax offset rate before any premium, in percent (s 355-100(1))?
GIVEN `aggregated turnover` IS A NUMBER @desc The company's aggregated turnover for the income year, in dollars
      `controlled by exempt entities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether exempt entities control the company as item 2 describes
      `corporate tax rate in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The company's corporate tax rate (25 for a base rate entity, else 30)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my company's R&D offset rate` MEANS
    IF `aggregated turnover` LESS THAN 20000000 AND NOT `controlled by exempt entities`
    THEN `corporate tax rate in percent` PLUS 185 DIVIDED BY 10
    ELSE `corporate tax rate in percent`

@export Is my company's R&D tax offset refundable (s 355-100 note 1, s 67-30)?
GIVEN `aggregated turnover` IS A NUMBER @desc The company's aggregated turnover for the income year, in dollars
      `controlled by exempt entities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether exempt entities control the company as item 2 describes
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my company's R&D offset refundable` IF
    `aggregated turnover` LESS THAN 20000000 AND NOT `controlled by exempt entities`

@export What refundable R&D tax offset does my small company get (s 355-100(1), (2))?
GIVEN `notional deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc The company's R&D deductions under the provisions s 355-100(1) lists, in dollars
      `research service provider and CRC expenditure` IS A NUMBER @desc The part paid to research service providers or as CRC contributions, in dollars
      `aggregated turnover` IS A NUMBER @desc The company's aggregated turnover for the income year, in dollars
      `corporate tax rate in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The company's corporate tax rate
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What R&D offset does my small company get` MEANS
    IF NOT `Is my company's R&D offset refundable` `aggregated turnover` FALSE THEN 0
    ELSE (IF `notional deductions` LESS THAN 20000 THEN `research service provider and CRC expenditure` ELSE `notional deductions`)
         TIMES `What is my company's R&D offset rate` `aggregated turnover` FALSE `corporate tax rate in percent`
         DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `360-15, 360-20, 360-25 -- early stage investor tax offset`

-- s 360-15(1): entitled if (among other things) a company that is an early stage innovation company (s 360-40) issues you
-- shares, you are not an affiliate, the shares are not ESS interests and you hold no more than 30% -- one fact here.
-- s 360-20(1): no entitlement if none of "subsections 708(8), (10) or (11) of the Corporations Act 2001 removed the need for a
-- disclosure document" and "a total of more than $50,000 was paid" for the shares in the income year.
-- s 360-25(1): "20% of the sum" of money and the market value of non-cash benefits received for the issue; (2) reduced so that the
-- offsets for the year and those carried forward, for you and your affiliates, do "not exceed $200,000".
@export What early stage investor tax offset do I get for shares issued to me this year (ss 360-15, 360-20, 360-25)?
GIVEN `the company and I meet s 360-15(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company is an early stage innovation company and you meet the other s 360-15(1) conditions
      `sophisticated or professional investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 708(8), (10) or (11) of the Corporations Act removed the need for a disclosure document
      `amount paid in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The total paid for the shares issued to you in the income year, in dollars
      `offsets already counted toward the cap` IS A NUMBER @desc Other offsets under Subdivision 360-A for you and your affiliates this year, including amounts carried forward
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What early stage investor tax offset do I get` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company and I meet s 360-15(1)`) OR ((NOT `sophisticated or professional investor`) AND `amount paid in the year` GREATER THAN 50000)
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the lesser of` (`amount paid in the year` TIMES 20 DIVIDED BY 100)
                         (`the greater of` (200000 MINUS `offsets already counted toward the cap`) 0)
